WEBVTT

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:24.910
Nah, she wouldn't screw up that bad.

00:02:28.740 --> 00:02:33.500
<i>You have an Alpha Stigma. That's quite valuable, you know.</i>

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.670
<i>I'll be sure to be careful when I crystallize it and take it from you.</i>

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:40.570
Crystallizing an Alpha Stigma, huh?

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.680
Could you be saved that way?

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.680
If it can save you, then before you hurt anybody...

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.890
Before your mind is damaged, I'll gouge it out myself.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.080
Where am I?

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:08.380
W-Who are you?!

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.580
Where are Dad and Mom?

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.240
Dad... Dad...

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.710
I-It's because of me that Dad and Mom are dead!

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.720
No, no, no! Everyone... I...

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.920
Y-You! You did that to Dad and Mom!

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.840
I'll kill you!

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.230
You're too slow.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.150
Why? Why me? What did I ever do?!

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.210
Just stop it! I can't take it anymore!

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:43.430
Why did this...

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:47.780
Why did this happen to Dad and Mom because of me?

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:51.110
Do you want to run? Or do you want to die?

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.020
I won't stop you.

00:03:53.020 --> 00:03:55.790
If you can be saved that way, then do as you like.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:58.210
You all want to kill me, don't you?!

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:02.250
A monster like me doesn't have any reason to exist!

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:06.510
Yeah. But...

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:12.770
I've thought about it a lot, too...

00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:19.370
Just being alive leads to those i hold dear to getting hurt, or killed.

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:22.350
And I get hated as taboo on top of that, as a monster.

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:24.940
Why is someone like me here?

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:26.570
Why was someone like me made?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:34.210
Wanted by no one, being hated and hurting others just for being alive.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:37.180
If that's all there is, I may as well die.

00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:40.290
I used to think about that constantly, all the time.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:45.550
But it was around that time that I found people who told me to live.

00:04:46.660 --> 00:04:50.550
Some curious king who knew I was a monster and still wanted me.

00:04:50.550 --> 00:04:55.120
Some person who struggled to persuade me that I was no monster.

00:04:55.630 --> 00:05:01.440
And lately, even someone who picks on me and calls me her manservent.

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:06.480
So I wonder if maybe there is some meaning for me.

00:05:07.450 --> 00:05:09.660
If maybe it's okay to live.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:13.290
So I dream of building a world,

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:17.030
one where they won't lose anything else.

00:05:19.070 --> 00:05:21.170
Listen to me, now I've started rambling.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:24.760
But I have no one left now...

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.880
No one who would want me to live.

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.880
What did your old man say before he died?

00:05:32.330 --> 00:05:35.210
Don't let it bother you if I get killed.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.850
You have to live...

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:40.850
Besides, you have someone waiting for you.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:46.190
The one who asked me to save you was a girl named Kuku.

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:47.420
Kuku?!

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:51.860
She's apparently being held captive as bait to lure you out.

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:56.220
So I'll have to go and save her. What'll you do?

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:58.610
I-I'll go and save her, too!

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.620
But, at the level you're at now...

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:05.140
I'll do whatever it takes to save Kuku! Please teach me, Mister!

00:06:05.420 --> 00:06:06.860
Watch out!

00:06:06.860 --> 00:06:08.050
Welcome back, Ferris.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:10.630
Arua, don't let yourself be fooled.

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:13.390
That man is a slacker who sleeps all day,

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:16.810
gets drunk on wine, brings misfortune to women,

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.150
and night after night, he goes out in town and...

00:06:20.910 --> 00:06:24.180
The rest cannot be said in front of children!

00:06:24.180 --> 00:06:26.240
Is that right, Mister Ryner?

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:29.650
Don't listen to her. Oh, this is my partner, Ferris.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:32.990
It's a pleasure to meet you!

00:06:35.880 --> 00:06:39.410
He's asking me to teach him how to fight, since he wants to rescue Kuku.

00:06:39.900 --> 00:06:43.210
Hmm. If I left it up to you, your perversion would rub off on him.

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:45.290
Come on, Arua. Let's go.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:46.710
Okay, Miss Ferris!

00:06:52.690 --> 00:06:54.610
He has Ferris teaching him martial arts,

00:06:54.610 --> 00:06:57.400
and he has the Alpha Stigma's magic capabilities.

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:03.260
He might grow into one hell of a master after this.

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.850
Hang in there, Arua.

00:07:16.720 --> 00:07:21.890
So, the story is supposed to have the hero Arua go and rescue the princess Kuku.

00:07:21.890 --> 00:07:23.040
Can you do it?

00:07:23.390 --> 00:07:25.870
Yes, I'll be sure to save Kuku.

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.800
That's what I've worked so hard for.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:31.250
You could die.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.850
Even so, I'm going! I'll go alone if I have to.

00:07:37.480 --> 00:07:40.220
Indeed, you've been raised well.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.530
As long as you don't resemble that good-for-nothing old man,

00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:43.520
all that hard work has paid off.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:46.900
I hope that's not referring to me.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.750
Who else is there?

00:07:48.750 --> 00:07:51.330
You've held the good-for-nothing world championship first-place title

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:53.490
for the past several centuries.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:55.890
I haven't lived that long!

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:05.660
No traps or ambushes?

00:08:05.660 --> 00:08:08.130
They've made complete fools out of us.

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:11.130
Yes, indeed! Of course we have!

00:08:11.490 --> 00:08:16.510
It's not as though anyone can stand up to my Ailecrono Scythe.

00:08:16.510 --> 00:08:19.640
My, my. We've been waiting for you.

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:22.060
Kuku is safe, I trust?

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:25.380
Of course. She's a valuable hostage, after all.

00:08:25.380 --> 00:08:28.290
To be honest, I didn't want to pull something like this,

00:08:28.290 --> 00:08:31.070
but brother Sui was so insistent this time.

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.160
You two can't win against me.

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.200
You should remember what happened last time.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.270
Yes, which is all the more reason we want your power.

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:41.930
Would you two be willing to surrender peacefully,

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:46.710
and use your power for the sake of our homeland, Gastark?

00:08:47.010 --> 00:08:48.080
Gastark?

00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:51.920
All the world will eventually belong to Gastark.

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:55.440
A peaceful world unified by an excellent king.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.840
A world where there is no discrimination, where no one gets hurt,

00:08:57.840 --> 00:09:02.350
where no one cries, where everyone can live happily.

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:07.300
The king of Gastark, our master Riphal Edea,

00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:09.440
is the vessel to create such a world.

00:09:10.730 --> 00:09:14.360
Your king sure sounds like an appealing guy.

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:15.660
Yes.

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:20.770
A world where no one gets hurt, where everyone can live happily?

00:09:20.770 --> 00:09:25.250
If your king can really create such a world,

00:09:25.250 --> 00:09:28.150
maybe it would be easier to join with you guys.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.160
Ryner.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:31.670
Then, with our country...

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:36.580
But if that's so, then why do you kill people?

00:09:36.580 --> 00:09:39.050
Why is it that all I see from you are dirty stunts like this?

00:09:40.070 --> 00:09:44.480
To have sole possession of Hero Relics, you kill huge numbers of people,

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:47.770
and you make an Alpha Stigma bearer go on a rampage to gouge out his eyes.

00:09:48.150 --> 00:09:50.720
Kill, kill, kill!

00:09:51.180 --> 00:09:55.690
If what you guys are doing is on the orders of the king of this so-called Gastark place,

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:58.900
your king's a piece of shit.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:02.130
That's not where I belong.

00:10:02.130 --> 00:10:03.610
At the very least,

00:10:03.610 --> 00:10:07.490
not in your country, where Alpha Stigma bearers aren't considered human beings.

00:10:08.330 --> 00:10:09.370
What'd you say?

00:10:10.560 --> 00:10:13.890
You're offering nothing but pretty words.

00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.090
You ask why we kill people? It's because it's necessary.

00:10:17.670 --> 00:10:21.240
We subdue kingdoms with the minimal necessary sacrifice.

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.200
It's not as though we enjoy what we do.

00:10:23.200 --> 00:10:26.600
When we kill people, we bear that pain...

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:30.020
You don't bear anything!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:36.490
Because of these "Eyes", I've killed tons of people who called me friend.

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:41.040
So there's no value in my being alive. That's what I've always thought.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.110
But Arua's different.

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.240
He hasn't killed anyone yet.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:50.550
He might not kill anyone after this, either.

00:10:51.000 --> 00:10:55.010
Yet you two are trying to kill him.

00:10:55.700 --> 00:10:59.710
He's not like me, no longer able to turn back.

00:10:59.710 --> 00:11:01.840
He still has a future.

00:11:02.140 --> 00:11:05.930
But you won't find a country anywhere

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:07.470
willing to accept an Alpha Stigma bearer.

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:10.470
Sorry, but Roland's actually different.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:14.500
Our king isn't like your king.

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:16.480
A country where everyone can live happily...

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:21.360
He's a genuine fool who seriously aims for that goal.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:26.490
After all, he's a greedy bastard who wants to save the small in addition to the large.

00:11:27.380 --> 00:11:30.440
He's an overly self-conscious guy who deludes himself into thinking he can do it,

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:36.000
and when anyone dies, he blames himself.

00:11:36.370 --> 00:11:40.210
But that's why I'm lending him a hand.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:43.920
Because if it's a world he builds, I'd be satisfied living in it.

00:11:44.330 --> 00:11:48.520
However, kings are always pressed with choices.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:50.870
Even if one can go without sacrifices in the present,

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:52.810
there's no telling how it could be in the future.

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:57.320
If that happens, I'll knock Sion upside the head and set him straight.

00:11:59.290 --> 00:12:01.110
Then we've reached a breakdown in negotiations.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:04.540
You had no room for negotiation to start with.

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:06.290
Now we'll be taking Kuku back.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:07.490
Let's move.

00:12:08.770 --> 00:12:11.300
That was a pretty good speech.

00:12:11.300 --> 00:12:13.250
I don't dislike that way of thinking, either.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:18.260
I'm putting my faith in you, partner.

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:20.680
Of course you are. I'll win.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.170
Yeah, of course!

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:23.840
Kuu!

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:37.650
Now then, let's make you disappear.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:51.920
I offer up this contract, to bear the wicked spirit beast which sleeps in the earth!

00:12:57.340 --> 00:13:00.380
It's still not too late. How about it?

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:02.590
Come to our country!

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:08.020
Like hell. What I seek is thunder!

00:13:08.430 --> 00:13:12.520
Do you think you can take on a Rule Fragment with ordinary magic?

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.020
Izuchi!

00:13:24.910 --> 00:13:25.910
Ice Wall!

00:13:36.900 --> 00:13:37.630
Burn her down!

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:38.920
Oh, no you don't!

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.010
From the direction of the west, the empty, the formation, the yang!

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:43.300
What I seek is thunder!

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:49.850
Izuchi!

00:13:50.160 --> 00:13:50.810
I bring forth brilliance... Damn it!

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:54.800
How could...

00:13:56.450 --> 00:13:57.770
I've lost.

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:07.950
There is one more enemy.

00:14:08.280 --> 00:14:10.490
Well, crap, that screws everything up.

00:14:10.490 --> 00:14:12.510
If we couldn't bring them down with this just now...

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.510
Yes, we're in a bit of trouble.

00:14:14.510 --> 00:14:17.410
Operation Surprise Attack was a failure. Call him back.

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:18.960
Arua!

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:20.590
Sir!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:25.220
Meddling with the magic structure, hm?

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:29.210
The boy fired that thunder from outside,

00:14:29.210 --> 00:14:31.350
and your magic formation allowed you to redirect its path.

00:14:31.870 --> 00:14:34.820
Yeesh, you saw through it that quick?

00:14:34.820 --> 00:14:36.810
I'd really rather not fight you.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:40.550
I should be saying that to you. The Alpha Stigma...

00:14:40.550 --> 00:14:44.950
Out of all of the Magic Eyes, I considered it a poor substitute of no significant level.

00:14:44.950 --> 00:14:47.490
But it's horribly troublesome.

00:14:48.010 --> 00:14:49.870
That doesn't sound much like praise.

00:14:50.250 --> 00:14:53.370
I realized it for the first time in this fight.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:56.500
I understand the reason why humans are in constant discord with you.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:15:00.500
They can't help but feel terrified by a monster beyond their imagination.

00:15:01.910 --> 00:15:04.010
We're the ones who are terrified the most.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:08.280
We're always terrified. We're always regretting being alive.

00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:12.400
Always, always shaking with the thought that we could hurt someone,

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:14.560
that we could kill someone.

00:15:14.800 --> 00:15:17.350
Then would you be so kind as to die?

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:20.820
If possible, I'd like to avoid fighting you ever again.

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:23.690
In that case, why don't you turn around and go home?

00:15:24.520 --> 00:15:25.700
Kuu.

00:15:31.870 --> 00:15:33.090
Kuku!

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.660
Don't tell me you're...

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:37.790
It's true that we can't win against you.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:43.770
So we'll kill this girl, and at least destroy that boy's sense of self.

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:44.970
Stop!

00:15:46.840 --> 00:15:48.390
You're too late!

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:52.850
Stop!

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.780
No... It can't be!

00:16:19.370 --> 00:16:24.240
Just now, that was a Rule Fragment of the same type as brother Lir's...

00:16:24.240 --> 00:16:25.880
Rule Fragments...

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:31.400
and Hero Relics, hm?

00:16:31.980 --> 00:16:36.850
Until recently, they were words beyond my knowledge.

00:16:43.280 --> 00:16:45.940
That's the man we met in Nelpha.

00:16:45.940 --> 00:16:47.240
What's he doing here?

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:49.740
Brother Sui, brother Sui!

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.920
Kuu, leave me and run!

00:16:51.920 --> 00:16:53.150
But... but...

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:57.910
So, is it you two who are instigating Runa's actions?

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.120
You went a bit too far.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:01.830
Let there be darkness!

00:17:03.180 --> 00:17:05.840
For crying out loud! What I seek is thunder! Izuchi!

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:16.460
Why? What I did to you was...

00:17:16.810 --> 00:17:18.970
I'll call in this favor one day. Go!

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:26.100
These circumstances are a bit hard to swallow.

00:17:26.840 --> 00:17:29.820
I listened in on your conversation.

00:17:30.440 --> 00:17:34.230
You two should be from Roland.

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:37.790
So why would you protect people of Gastark?

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.540
We're not like you.

00:17:40.540 --> 00:17:42.480
Eliminating others because they're obstacles.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.540
If you keep repeating that, what would be left?

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:50.960
<i>Alpha Stigma, Hero Relics... What is His Majesty planning?</i>

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:56.090
Hold on, what? Are you leaving?

00:17:57.460 --> 00:18:01.350
I see no need to fight with you two right now.

00:18:03.350 --> 00:18:06.360
It may sound intrusive,

00:18:06.810 --> 00:18:09.960
but may I offer you one warning?

00:18:09.960 --> 00:18:11.360
Huh? Warning?

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.990
You just asked what would be left

00:18:15.990 --> 00:18:19.120
after continually removing obstacles.

00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:23.940
In my sincere belief, if I keep eliminating obstacles,

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:29.240
what will be left at the end will be people who are convenient to me.

00:18:29.850 --> 00:18:34.810
And for you, as an Alpha Stigma bearer, the result of killing all humans

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:38.140
would be making a world much easier for Alpha Stigma bearers to live in.

00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:41.020
That is the truth, is it not?

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:44.520
Humans are animals that can't live without conflict.

00:18:44.930 --> 00:18:50.150
Everyone being able to live happily, with no sacrifices? It's nonsense.

00:18:50.150 --> 00:18:52.570
As long as they don't have painful experiences...

00:18:52.570 --> 00:18:55.380
No, you're an Alpha Stigma bearer.

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:58.960
You would know the ugliness of humans better than anyone else.

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:03.040
I have truly spoken intrusively.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:08.040
You were a big help this time. Thanks for saving Kuku.

00:19:09.130 --> 00:19:11.790
Do you seriously claim I saved that girl?

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:14.670
No, I doubt that,

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:18.870
but that timing definitely gave them a good opening.

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.140
What a pity.

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:25.340
I suppose I really will end up killing you someday.

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:28.670
Your existence is extremely...

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.240
Kuku! Kuku!

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:38.520
Arua!

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.950
What do we do now?

00:19:39.950 --> 00:19:43.830
Well, we can't take them with us to search for Hero Relics.

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:48.080
I've got it! I know just the person.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:55.090
All right, I'll leave it to them!

00:20:03.100 --> 00:20:04.930
I'd better set out a light.

00:20:05.760 --> 00:20:08.940
You truly do love to agonize over things, don't you?

00:20:09.740 --> 00:20:11.440
War is brewing.

00:20:12.530 --> 00:20:15.220
The Runa Empire's acting strange.

00:20:15.220 --> 00:20:18.450
It's rumored that there are signs that a revolution is starting in Nelpha.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.160
Now that the world has begun to move, there is no stopping it.

00:20:22.640 --> 00:20:25.720
If things stay like this, conflict will become inevitable.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.460
Even though no one wishes for that.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:32.270
I wonder about that. People kill each other.

00:20:32.270 --> 00:20:35.880
For self-defense, for a happy future,

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:38.380
for the dreams and ideals they embrace.

00:20:38.380 --> 00:20:44.390
and all of those dreams and ideals they embrace are entrusted to you, the king.

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:49.890
I want to answer them. The people's wishes, their hopes...

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:53.730
A world without war, where all can live happily.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.960
One where no one and nothing is lost.

00:20:57.960 --> 00:21:02.870
I want to make a world where people can just take afternoon naps all day.

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:08.000
And so you continue to gaze at the dream furthest from reality.

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:11.890
Even though you're well aware that it could never happen.

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.850
It should still be in sight.

00:21:16.850 --> 00:21:19.080
It should still be achievable.

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:23.590
Still, still, still...

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:29.470
I made a promise. I made a promise to him.

00:21:29.470 --> 00:21:35.520
So, I must set out a light...

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:40.080
A light...

00:23:20.410 --> 00:23:23.000
<i>You know, I just realized it.</i>

00:23:23.000 --> 00:23:25.620
<i>All of these pain-in-the-ass situations I keep getting into,</i>

00:23:25.620 --> 00:23:27.960
<i>they're all Sion's fault, aren't they?</i>

00:23:27.960 --> 00:23:31.480
<i>Damn it, you diabolical, arrogant bastard!</i>

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:34.930
<i>Witness my pain-in-the-ass power!</i>
